# Get started

To get started with Giolt, first add the Giolt SDK to your project:

```
$ gleam add giolt_sdk
```

The Giolt SDK is a library, not a CLI — it has no commands of its own. Scaffold your
build, deploy and dev scripts with its one-shot generator:

```
$ gleam run -m giolt_sdk/init
```

This writes `build.gleam`, `deploy.gleam` and `{project}_dev.gleam` into your `src/`
directory. Compile your project, then build your app by running:

```
$ gleam run -m build
```

With an entry module configured in `build.gleam`, this creates a `./dist` folder
containing the entrypoint to your app.

[Read the full Giolt SDK reference](/sdk)

